Soundbite builds on Audiogram (github.com/drkxbt/audiogram, MIT) for the editor and the video, and on
transformers.js (Hugging Face, Apache-2.0) with ONNX Runtime Web (Microsoft, MIT) for speech recognition. The speech
model, Whisper by OpenAI (MIT), converted to ONNX by the onnx-community, is downloaded from Hugging Face when it is
first needed and is not part of this repository.

The demo page ships the Geist and Geist Mono typefaces by Vercel, in collaboration with basement.studio, in
demo/fonts/, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (demo/fonts/OFL.txt). The sample in demo/sample is Audiogram's
made-up exchange read by the Microsoft David and Microsoft Zira text-to-speech voices; it is not a recording of any
real Space or person.

The editor's fonts come from Fontsource under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, each one's licence copied next to it in
dist/app/fonts/. The ornaments in the podcast designs are drawn in ornaments.ts for this project. The photos in photos/
are in the public domain (CC0), found through Openverse; photos/CREDITS.md credits each one's photographer.

X is named only to say what the clips are for; X Corp. has no connection with this project. Google Ad Manager serves
the optional rewarded ad on drk.vc's copy; Google has no connection with this project either.
